    "id": "x4_low_difference_johnson_highwidth_bound",
    "title": "Low-difference local SP Johnson high-width bound",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For a fixed base support, side-width-e neighbours whose reduced locator difference has degree at most d have changed 2e-sets with pairwise intersection at most e+d. Hence their number is at most N(e-d)/(4e^2-N(e+d)) whenever the denominator is positive. At N=2^41 and d=1, every width e>=N/4+1 has at most N^2/16 records, and summing all at most N/4 such widths costs at most N^3/64. Thus only t_XR+2<=e<=N/4 remains in the d=1 branch.",
